    "body": "## Motivation\n\nSince #42175, `Qwen4ExpLayerExtensionMixin.__init__` imports `sglang.srt.layers.moe.qwen4_decode` unconditionally. That module imports `custom_all_reduce_v2`, which imports `tvm_ffi`. The XPU install (`pyproject_xpu.toml`) does not provide `tvm_ffi`, so Qwen4Exp (Qwen3.8-Flash-Next) models fail during layer construction on Intel GPUs:\n\n```\nFile \".../sglang/srt/layers/moe/qwen4_decode.py\", line 15, in <module>\n    from sglang.srt.distributed.device_communicators.custom_all_reduce_v2 import (\nFile \".../sglang/srt/distributed/device_communicators/custom_all_reduce_v2.py\", line 35, in <module>\n    from sglang.kernels.ops.communication.all_reduce import (\nFile \".../sglang/kernels/ops/communication/all_reduce.py\", line 7, in <module>\n    import tvm_ffi\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'tvm_ffi'\n```\n\n`prepare_qwen4_decode_comm` already returns `None` unless the device is CUDA SM10, so the import is not needed on other platforms.\n\n## Modifications\n\nGate the import and the `prepare_qwen4_decode_comm` call on `is_cuda()`. CUDA behaviour is unchanged. The second import in `_run_ffn_stage` is only reached when `_decode_moe_comm` is not `None`, so it needs no change.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nNo change to model outputs on CUDA. The non-CUDA path was already `_decode_moe_comm = None`.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNot performance-related. Tested on 1x Intel Arc Pro B70 (torch 2.14.0+xpu, sglang-kernel-xpu 0.4.0) with a 4-layer dummy-weight Qwen3.8-Flash-Next config (`--load-format dummy --device xpu --attention-backend intel_xpu`). Before this change, the server failed at model construction with the error above. After it, the server starts and serves eager decode at C1/C2/C4.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit). (ruff check / ruff format / isort pass on the changed file)\n- [ ] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [ ] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38790871227](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38790871227)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38790871010](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38790871010)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38790871079](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38790871079)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
